      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "Given that  $(3{w}^{2}+w+5)({w}^{2}+w+1)=3{w}^{4}+a{w}^{3}+b{w}^{2}+cw+5,$ calculate $a+b+c.$",
      "worked_solution": "We distribute all three terms of the trinomial in the first set of parentheses to the trinomial in the second set of parentheses. Then, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3{w}^{2}+w+5)({w}^{2}+w+1) & = \\\\ 3{w}^{2}({w}^{2}+w+1)+w({w}^{2}+w+1)+5({w}^{2}+w+1) & = \\\\ 3{w}^{4}+3{w}^{3}+3{w}^{2}+{w}^{3}+{w}^{2}+w+5{w}^{2}+5w+5 & = \\\\ 3{w}^{4}+4{w}^{3}+9{w}^{2}+6w+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=4,$ $b=9,$ and $c=6.$ So, \n\n$$\na+b+c=4+9+6=19.\n$$",
